 Deriving the regen and the check from ONE\n+# declaration is the WI-260 \"gate and scheduler read one rule\" precedent applied\n+# to disposition-vs-floor: a new generated projection cannot join the floor\n+# without also joining this list, and the two cannot pick different flags —\n+# tests/test_agent_dispatch_decisions.py::test_disposition_regen_tracks_floor\n+# pins each entry to its floor step's command.\n+#\n+# Deliberately a SUBSET of the floor's freshness steps: arch-map (the code map),\n+# derived-gate, and skills-sync are floor-checked too, but a disposition edits\n+# none of THEIR inputs (no source, no gate ratification, no skill source), so\n+# regenerating them would be pure churn. That subset judgment is the recorded\n+# divergence (WI-283 done-when): the binding test tripwires on any change to the\n+# floor's step list so the call is revisited when the floor grows a gate.\n+#\n+# Each entry opts in per artifact on a marker path (`.exists()`), so a non-adopter\n+# of that artifact regenerates nothing.\n+#   (floor_step, generator, flags, opt_in_markers)\n+_DISPOSITION_REGEN = (\n+    (\"okf\", \"gen_okf.py\", (), (\"docs/okf\",)),\n+    (\"trajectory-map\", \"gen_trajectory.py\", (), (\"PROJECT_STATE.html\",)),\n+    (\"status-map\", \"gen_trajectory.py\", (\"--status\",), _STATUS_MAP_MARKERS),\n+)\n+\n+\n def _regenerate_disposition_artifacts(worktree):\n-    \"\"\"Regenerate freshness-gated views after a disposition edits registries.\n+    \"\"\"Regenerate the freshness-gated views a disposition stales, in the staging\n+    worktree, before its commit — so the commit passes the same pre-commit floor\n+    the harness runs (see `_DISPOSITION_REGEN`, single-homed with that floor).\n \n     The generators are kit-owned siblings of this dispatcher even when the\n-    checkout is a downstream scaffold. Artifact presence is the opt-in signal:\n-    a non-adopter must not depend on either generator.\n+    checkout is a downstream scaffold. Artifact presence is the opt-in signal: a\n+    non-adopter (no marker) regenerates nothing, so it never depends on a\n+    generator it did not adopt. Order matters — okf feeds the dashboard.\n     \
