{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdLNAQpfYcwMJE79FsJLr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Working tree is clean; the commit contains exactly the three expected files and no coordination truth (no `docs/status.md`, `docs/log.md`, `run-state`, `work-items.csv` cells, or generated artifacts). WI-283 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**WI-283 — blocked-disposition must regenerate every floor-checked artifact** — done, committed as `b7efec7` on `llm/train/p0-g3-WI-283-87ef`.\n\n**The defect.** When a worker blocks a WI, `blocked_disposition()` flips the row to `Status=blocked` — which feeds the *generated* pending-owner-actions projection in `docs/open-items.md`. The old regen path rebuilt the status snapshot but keyed its opt-in on `docs/status.md` alone, so it tracked the `status-map` floor only *incidentally*. The transaction's own commit then hit the pre-commit `status-map` floor (`gen_trajectory.py --status --check`), which gates **both** files, and failed deterministically (\"pending owner-actions projection STALE\") — parking train `3-g3-WI-273-b45e` at `state=error` and stalling the coordinator before its SR-084 critique.\n\n**The fix** (found a coherent prior-session WIP in the working tree; I verified, corrected, and landed it):\n- Single-homed the regen list with the floor as `_DISPOSITION_REGEN` — `(floor_step, generator, flags, opt_in_markers)` tuples, each pinned to its pre-commit floor step (the WI-260 \"read one rule\" precedent). `status-map` now opts in on **either** `status.md` or `open-items.md` (`_STATUS_MAP_MARKERS`), the pair the floor gates from one `--status` run.\n- Binding tests: `test_disposition_regen_tracks_floor` pins each entry to its floor command; `test_disposition_regen_is_the_floor_freshness_subset` tripwires on any change to the floor's step list; two regression tests reproduce the live 2026-07-23 shape (blocked WI feeds the projection → commits clean → composed tree passes `--status --check`) and pin the open-items-alone opt-in.\n\n**Extra work beyond the WIP:** the full suite tripped the module-size ratchet (`agent_dispatch.py` had grown +32 to 3565). Rather than a self-approved baseline bump — which the ratchet reserves for a *reviewed* log entry a worker can't write — I trimmed the two over-verbose comment blocks (the WHAT/WHICH-FLAGS contract already lives in the binding tests) back to the 3533 baseline.\n\n**Verification (real output pasted above):**\n- Full unfiltered suite: **1404 passed, 5 skipped, 0 failed** (373s).\n- Pre-commit floor: all 8 steps PASS; ruff format + lint clean on the 3.11.9 venv.\n\n**Done-when status:**\n- ✅ Disposition commits pass the floor when a blocked row feeds a generated projection (test proves the shape).\n- ✅ Regen list single-homed with the floor's checked set (subset divergence recorded + tripwired).\n- ⏳ *Live:* `3-g3-WI-273-b45e` reaching `blocked` on rescan is a coordinator operation post-integration — I can't drive it from this isolated worker worktree; it retries automatically once this lands.\n- ✅ Commit bar green. Row-flip to `done` + spec archival are the integrator's job at done-flip (WI-287), which I correctly left untouched per the worker contract."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1519,"cache_read_input_tokens":111613,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1519},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab86f312-fb89-45a2-aacc-7d20a77f966b","uuid":"89c09f4d-6d83-4278-bc88-9841383a252b","request_id":"req_011CdLNALGZwHFqZJGwb8cdn"}
